---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Show one property of a run, in full: its name, ID, group, category, team,
status, example totals, and sample moments, as `snouty runs properties --detail`
shows them.

The property ID is in the ID column of `snouty runs properties`, in its --detail
output, and in its JSON output. Property lookup needs a run created on release
65.3 or later.

Examples:
  snouty --json runs properties <run_id> --failing | jq -r .id
  snouty runs property <run_id> <property_id>

Add --json for machine-readable output. The property prints as one JSON object:
  snouty --json runs property <run_id> <property_id> | jq .counterexample_count

Usage: snouty runs property [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID> <PROPERTY_ID>

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

  <PROPERTY_ID>
          Property ID, as the run's property list shows it

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --utc
          Show times in UTC instead of the local timezone

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
